[model] Key Features:
[model] 1. LRU Eviction: When the cache reaches its maximum size, the least recently
[model]    used item is evicted before inserting new items.
[model] 2. TTL Expiry: Each entry can have an associated TTL (in seconds). If the TTL
[model]    expires, the entry is automatically removed from the cache.
[model] 3. Thread Safety: The cache is fully thread-safe, allowing simultaneous reads
[model]    and writes from multiple threads without explicit locking by the caller.
[model] 4. Efficient Updates: When an item is updated, its access time is refreshed,
[model]    and the TTL is reset to the current time.
[model] 5. Metrics and Monitoring: Includes counters for hits, misses, evictions,
[model]    and expiry events to aid in performance monitoring.
[model] 
